WEBVTT

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:22.560
"Taisho Otome Fairy Tale"

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:32.050
"Taisho Otome Fairy Tale"

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:37.010
"Episode 11"
"In Search of Yuzuki"

00:01:42.390 --> 00:01:45.560
I'll go to Tokyo. And then...

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:47.890
...Yuzu and I <i>will </i>come home together!

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:50.480
Tamahiko-<i>sensei</i>!

00:01:51.610 --> 00:01:53.980
Hey, gang! You're all right!

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:56.360
Tamahiko... I'm going, too.

00:01:58.110 --> 00:02:00.450
I'm worried about Ryotaro!

00:02:00.450 --> 00:02:03.870
If our little village was hit this hard,

00:02:03.870 --> 00:02:07.750
how much worse must it be in Tokyo?

00:02:07.750 --> 00:02:09.120
She's thinking the same thing.

00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:13.290
So please--let me go with you!

00:02:13.290 --> 00:02:17.050
But what about Keita and Yamato?

00:02:17.050 --> 00:02:20.430
We've got the others--we'll be fine!

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:21.510
Jus' fine!

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:25.930
We're worried about our brother, too.

00:02:25.930 --> 00:02:28.690
Yeah, but still...

00:02:28.690 --> 00:02:31.350
Are your families and
the other villagers all right?

00:02:32.610 --> 00:02:35.780
Actually... a lot of people got hurt.

00:02:35.780 --> 00:02:39.320
Most houses collapsed--or burned.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:41.740
The clinic's been destroyed, too.

00:02:41.740 --> 00:02:45.240
My gramps is sick,
but he's sleeping outdoors.

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:49.410
Okay, here's what we'll do.

00:02:49.410 --> 00:02:53.790
Find your families and
any villager without a home

00:02:53.790 --> 00:02:55.630
and bring them to my house.

00:02:57.260 --> 00:02:58.470
It's all right.

00:02:58.470 --> 00:03:01.050
The grown-ups in the village may balk,

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:04.800
but my grandfather built
the place to be extra-sturdy.

00:03:04.800 --> 00:03:07.270
Help yourself to the
medicine cabinet and food.

00:03:07.270 --> 00:03:11.060
If you can promise me
that everyone will be safe,

00:03:11.060 --> 00:03:13.480
I'll take Ryo with me.

00:03:13.480 --> 00:03:14.810
Tamahiko...

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:17.150
Well? Can you do that for me?

00:03:17.150 --> 00:03:18.820
We can!

00:03:18.820 --> 00:03:22.240
I'm the mayor's son--I'll work hard!

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:23.450
Great!

00:03:23.450 --> 00:03:26.160
Thank you, Tamahiko-<i>sensei</i>!

00:03:26.160 --> 00:03:29.450
Make sure you come home
with Miss Yuzu, okay?

00:03:29.450 --> 00:03:30.870
I will!

00:03:30.870 --> 00:03:33.460
See you later!

00:03:33.460 --> 00:03:35.920
--Good luck, Sis!
--Be careful, you two!

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:37.920
Say hi to Ryotaro!

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:41.630
How far are we going today?

00:03:41.630 --> 00:03:44.260
As far as we can walk before nightfall.

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:47.850
It's a good 30 <i>ri </i>to Tokyo.

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:50.560
We'll probably arrive around
noon the day after tomorrow.

00:03:52.850 --> 00:03:55.150
If you want to turn back, now's the time.

00:03:56.940 --> 00:04:01.280
Don't be stupid. For Ryotaro?
I'll walk as far as it takes!

00:04:10.830 --> 00:04:15.040
For a rich kid, you sure are
comfortable sleeping in the rough.

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:17.040
Oh, I'm not.

00:04:17.040 --> 00:04:20.460
But it's no hardship if I think of Yuzu.

00:04:20.460 --> 00:04:21.590
Same as you.

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:24.800
I guess so.

00:04:24.800 --> 00:04:28.510
If it means I get to see Ryotaro,
this is nothing.

00:04:28.510 --> 00:04:32.390
You have a soft spot
for all your brothers,

00:04:32.390 --> 00:04:35.100
but especially for Ryotaro, it seems.

00:04:35.100 --> 00:04:37.150
Well, sure.

00:04:37.150 --> 00:04:42.070
Ryotaro safeguarded
something precious to me.

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:49.280
What's with this lumpy rice ball?

00:04:49.280 --> 00:04:53.330
I made it. Sorry it's misshapen.

00:04:53.330 --> 00:04:57.750
But I got the pickled plum
in there all right, didn't I?

00:04:57.750 --> 00:05:00.250
I guess I have no choice, huh?

00:05:07.760 --> 00:05:08.760
Well?

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:10.100
Wow.

00:05:10.100 --> 00:05:13.060
This tastes just awful.

00:05:13.060 --> 00:05:15.190
I'm tearing up over here.

00:05:15.190 --> 00:05:17.270
A-Are you really?

00:05:23.990 --> 00:05:26.490
I hear it's even worse in Tokyo.

00:05:26.490 --> 00:05:28.660
Fires breaking out in
the blink of an eye...

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:32.830
"2 People Inside--Please Help"

00:05:28.660 --> 00:05:32.830
Nihonbashi, Asakusa,
and Kanda got the worst of it.

00:05:32.830 --> 00:05:36.210
Tokyo is a hell on earth.
I'd keep my distance.

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:40.790
Let's hurry.

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:48.550
I want to see Yuzu... as soon as possible.

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:52.180
You get tough when Yuzu's involved, huh.

00:05:52.180 --> 00:05:53.970
You think?

00:05:53.970 --> 00:05:57.770
Yeah. You're tough--really strong.

00:05:57.770 --> 00:05:59.980
I'm pushing myself, that's all.

00:05:59.980 --> 00:06:03.980
Every time I hear what it's like in Tokyo,
my heart feels like it's about to break.

00:06:06.190 --> 00:06:12.030
I had no idea. I'd never
treasured anyone before.

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:14.830
To think losing someone
could be so terrifying.

00:06:16.660 --> 00:06:19.040
Now I'm trusting in Yuzu,

00:06:19.040 --> 00:06:22.000
screwing up what little courage I have.

00:06:24.630 --> 00:06:31.510
I wondered if my big sister, had she
lived, would have been so kind to me.

00:06:33.970 --> 00:06:39.310
I'd like to show that people-pleaser
a thing or two myself--

00:06:39.310 --> 00:06:42.560
like the genuine goodness
of an older sister.

00:06:44.150 --> 00:06:47.030
I've got to show her
Big Sis Ryo--in earnest.

00:06:47.030 --> 00:06:51.110
What, are you going to have
her calling you "big sis" now?

00:06:51.110 --> 00:06:56.660
Ooh, good idea!
And <i>you </i>could call me that, too.

00:06:56.660 --> 00:06:58.580
I'll pass.

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:00.580
Now, don't be shy!

00:07:07.010 --> 00:07:10.090
Is this... is this really Tokyo?

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:18.390
The only thing still standing
around here is Tokyo Station.

00:07:18.390 --> 00:07:20.890
That's where everyone is taking shelter.

00:07:22.270 --> 00:07:23.940
Yuzu...

00:07:23.940 --> 00:07:24.940
Yuzu!

00:07:25.730 --> 00:07:26.570
Yuzu!

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:28.990
Yuzu!

00:07:32.530 --> 00:07:34.370
Yuzu!

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:35.530
Yuzu!

00:07:39.040 --> 00:07:39.870
Yuz--

00:07:41.410 --> 00:07:43.540
It <i>is </i>you! I knew it!

00:07:43.540 --> 00:07:45.420
Tamako?!

00:07:45.420 --> 00:07:46.960
Why are you here?

00:07:46.960 --> 00:07:49.170
Tamako--Yuzu--

00:07:52.470 --> 00:07:54.550
--Brother?!
--Tamahiko!

00:08:07.270 --> 00:08:09.650
Tamahiko--you're awake.

00:08:10.860 --> 00:08:14.360
Uncle Tamasuke... what are you doing here?

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:19.490
Medical relief groups from throughout
Japan have come to Tokyo.

00:08:19.490 --> 00:08:22.910
Almost all of the city's hospitals
have burned down.

00:08:24.500 --> 00:08:26.330
Your friend told me what's going on.

00:08:28.000 --> 00:08:30.010
I have to look for Yuzu.

00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:32.630
You need to rest a while longer.

00:08:32.630 --> 00:08:34.840
Didn't you walk here from Chiba?

00:08:34.840 --> 00:08:37.010
I can't just lie around!

00:08:37.010 --> 00:08:38.760
Tamahiko.

00:08:38.760 --> 00:08:41.390
This may sound cruel,

00:08:41.390 --> 00:08:46.810
but finding one solitary young woman
in Tokyo right now will be difficult.

00:08:46.810 --> 00:08:50.440
With nothing to go on,
you're bound to fail.

00:08:51.820 --> 00:08:56.820
I'm here because I believe
that I <i>will </i>find her.

00:08:56.820 --> 00:08:59.450
Yuzu <i>is </i>alive.

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:02.950
What is it?

00:09:02.950 --> 00:09:07.460
It's just... you've changed, Tamahiko.

00:09:07.460 --> 00:09:12.340
When I operated on your arm,
you had this look in your eyes:

00:09:12.340 --> 00:09:14.510
like you trusted nothing and no one.

00:09:16.130 --> 00:09:19.430
And it's not just you--it's Tamako, too.

00:09:19.430 --> 00:09:22.180
Meeting Yuzu changed you both.

00:09:24.430 --> 00:09:27.150
I'd like to meet her myself.

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:29.020
I hope you find her.

00:09:29.020 --> 00:09:29.980
Right.

00:09:31.610 --> 00:09:33.530
Okay: shall we?

00:09:33.530 --> 00:09:36.400
Yeah. I'll check out Asakusa.

00:09:36.400 --> 00:09:38.490
That's where Ryotaro was working.

00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:42.120
I'll try Ueno.
We can walk together for a while.

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:45.080
They've opened a free
maternity clinic there;

00:09:45.080 --> 00:09:47.870
a worried Midori-<i>san </i>could
be headed that way.

00:09:49.710 --> 00:09:50.840
Brother!

00:09:54.050 --> 00:09:57.380
I'll help look for Yuzu, too!

00:09:57.380 --> 00:09:58.510
Huh?

00:09:58.510 --> 00:10:01.510
Uncle gave me permission and everything.

00:10:01.510 --> 00:10:06.060
I... I'm worried about Yuzu, too.

00:10:07.640 --> 00:10:08.480
Tamako...

00:10:10.150 --> 00:10:12.360
Thanks. We can use the help.

00:10:15.320 --> 00:10:17.900
We'll meet up at Tokyo Station
this evening.

00:10:17.900 --> 00:10:19.950
Right. Be careful.

00:10:19.950 --> 00:10:21.490
Work hard, gang!

00:10:25.700 --> 00:10:29.420
Two girls, about 15 years old?

00:10:29.420 --> 00:10:31.920
No, they haven't come here.

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:33.170
I see...

00:10:38.510 --> 00:10:42.760
Is there a Sonoko Kihara
from Ozuna, Yokohama?

00:10:42.760 --> 00:10:45.100
Anyone know where Kinko Kurishima is?

00:10:45.100 --> 00:10:48.940
Has anyone seen Ito Nishikado
of Honjo Ward?

00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:52.440
Is Seiichiro Arai of Sakuragi here?

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:57.440
"In search of Ozo Sasaki-<i>sensei</i>
of Funabashi, Chiba"
"Deceased"

00:10:57.440 --> 00:10:58.900
"Deceased"

00:10:59.360 --> 00:11:00.280
Tamahiko...

00:11:00.280 --> 00:11:02.410
Yeah... right.

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:08.370
Shouldn't we hang that higher up?

00:11:10.210 --> 00:11:12.790
This is about eye-level for Yuzu.

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:13.880
Aha.

00:11:13.920 --> 00:11:19.920
"Yuzuki"
"Tamahiko is at the first-aid site in Tokyo Station
If you see this, come at once"

00:11:25.600 --> 00:11:28.180
"Bedding Distribution Center"

00:11:53.920 --> 00:11:58.380
I hear Yoshiwara is full of burned
corpses and drowning victims.

00:11:58.380 --> 00:12:02.050
So many, in fact, that they're
cremating them on site.

00:12:02.050 --> 00:12:06.760
Those poor people. If that happened
to a woman I loved, it'd hit hard.

00:12:14.520 --> 00:12:16.020
Brother?

00:12:16.020 --> 00:12:19.280
If... if Yuzu is dead...

00:12:19.280 --> 00:12:20.740
I'll die, too.

00:12:22.490 --> 00:12:25.570
If Yuzu is... if she's already...

00:12:28.660 --> 00:12:35.580
No way! The Yuzu I know wouldn't
die and leave you all alone!

00:12:35.580 --> 00:12:39.920
No matter how much I love my big sister...

00:12:39.920 --> 00:12:43.220
I'd <i>never </i>forgive her
for leaving you behind!

00:12:43.220 --> 00:12:45.590
Never, <i>ever</i>!

00:12:45.590 --> 00:12:52.140
You and Yuzu just have
to be together--you <i>have </i>to!

00:12:52.140 --> 00:12:57.310
I... I wanna see Yuzu, too!

00:12:59.070 --> 00:13:04.030
She's been putting on a brave front
for me, but she <i>is </i>only 13.

00:13:04.030 --> 00:13:07.990
I just <i>had </i>to whine to her--
and now I've made her cry.

00:13:09.030 --> 00:13:10.790
What a shameful older brother.

00:13:12.290 --> 00:13:14.370
I'm sorry, Tamako.

00:13:14.370 --> 00:13:15.620
Brother...

00:13:18.590 --> 00:13:21.960
Fine. Pet my head all you want.

00:13:21.960 --> 00:13:23.090
Thank you.

00:13:24.970 --> 00:13:27.970
Let's head back.
We'll look again tomorrow.

00:13:30.310 --> 00:13:32.770
Holding hands again?

00:13:32.770 --> 00:13:36.390
I'm just pulling my
wimpy ol' brother along!

00:13:39.110 --> 00:13:41.320
I'm fine, really.

00:13:41.320 --> 00:13:42.570
Too bad!

00:13:45.490 --> 00:13:46.490
What's wrong?

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:47.860
There--

00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:49.700
that woman over there.

00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:52.240
She's acting strange...

00:13:53.500 --> 00:13:54.540
Don't tell me--

00:13:58.040 --> 00:14:00.170
You mustn't be hasty!

00:14:00.170 --> 00:14:02.500
Don't throw your life away!

00:14:02.500 --> 00:14:06.720
You've got it all wrong!
I was only saying a prayer!

00:14:06.720 --> 00:14:07.720
Eh?

00:14:09.180 --> 00:14:12.970
I would never <i>dream </i>of ending it all!

00:14:12.970 --> 00:14:14.890
"For Ease in Childbirth"

00:14:12.970 --> 00:14:14.890
Not with this baby in my belly...

00:14:18.400 --> 00:14:19.400
Midori-<i>san</i>?!

00:14:29.610 --> 00:14:32.030
It... can't be...

00:14:32.030 --> 00:14:35.120
Tamahiko-<i>san</i>?! You're Tamahiko-<i>san</i>!

00:14:35.120 --> 00:14:38.870
Yes, I am! Tamahiko Shima!

00:14:38.870 --> 00:14:43.840
You're Midori-<i>san</i>, right? To think
we're meeting here, of all places!

00:14:43.840 --> 00:14:45.590
And Yuzu?

00:14:51.090 --> 00:14:53.300
As it happens...

00:14:53.300 --> 00:14:54.930
...we got separated.

00:14:56.980 --> 00:15:00.770
We were together for a while,
dodging fires as we ran.

00:15:02.810 --> 00:15:03.940
Midori-<i>san</i>!

00:15:05.820 --> 00:15:07.030
Yuzuki-<i>san</i>!

00:15:10.110 --> 00:15:13.620
I lost consciousness at some point.

00:15:13.620 --> 00:15:17.040
When I came to, I was at a first-aid site.

00:15:17.040 --> 00:15:23.290
But Yuzuki-<i>san </i>wasn't
the one who'd brought me in.

00:15:23.290 --> 00:15:26.130
Then... Yuzu is...

00:15:26.130 --> 00:15:30.680
I'm so sorry. If only I hadn't
said I'd wanted to see her...

00:15:30.680 --> 00:15:34.100
This is all my fault... all my fault...

00:15:35.720 --> 00:15:39.100
Please don't say that.

00:15:39.100 --> 00:15:44.150
Yuzu was so, so excited to see you.

00:15:46.730 --> 00:15:48.990
Is your baby all right?

00:15:48.990 --> 00:15:51.110
Y-Yes.

00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:52.950
That's good.

00:15:52.950 --> 00:15:56.910
I'll take it from here.
You wait somewhere safe.

00:15:56.910 --> 00:15:59.410
Tamako, take care of Midori-<i>san</i>.

00:15:59.410 --> 00:16:00.460
Huh?

00:16:00.460 --> 00:16:04.920
It's all right--I'll find her.
I know I will.

00:16:06.800 --> 00:16:08.710
Please do.

00:16:08.710 --> 00:16:12.760
I'll be waiting for Yuzu's return!

00:16:14.510 --> 00:16:15.390
Right!

00:16:24.850 --> 00:16:29.150
Yuzu... you must have
witnessed hell itself.

00:16:30.940 --> 00:16:33.660
Tokyo, that beautiful city...

00:16:33.660 --> 00:16:36.030
People smiling with delight...

00:16:36.030 --> 00:16:37.490
All of it, turned to ash.

00:16:40.910 --> 00:16:44.080
She was found in the rubble
of a collapsed building.

00:16:44.080 --> 00:16:46.460
When she came to us, she was already...

00:16:51.800 --> 00:16:53.930
It... it's not her.

00:17:00.180 --> 00:17:03.640
How many days has it been since the quake?

00:17:03.640 --> 00:17:06.440
I've never been away
from Yuzu for this long.

00:17:07.480 --> 00:17:12.780
If not for the quake, I'd be home
eating Yuzu's cooking right now.

00:17:13.740 --> 00:17:18.410
The rice balls she makes
with her tiny hands are so small,

00:17:18.410 --> 00:17:20.040
but so tasty.

00:17:33.800 --> 00:17:35.380
Kotori-<i>chan</i>?

00:17:35.380 --> 00:17:37.930
Well! If it isn't Shima-<i>kun</i>!

00:17:39.180 --> 00:17:42.850
Greetings! It's me:
the handsome young Hakaru-<i>kun</i>!

00:17:42.850 --> 00:17:44.890
Wha... huh?!

00:17:44.890 --> 00:17:46.230
But <i>why</i>?

00:17:46.230 --> 00:17:49.770
Times like these are made
for helping one another.

00:17:49.770 --> 00:17:54.780
Kotori-<i>chan</i>'s going around Tokyo
singing--to lift everyone's spirits.

00:17:55.990 --> 00:17:57.820
She's handing out rations, too.

00:17:57.820 --> 00:18:01.240
And since folks are drawn to her,
she's finding people.

00:18:02.830 --> 00:18:04.750
Me? I'm helping!

00:18:05.660 --> 00:18:08.330
What?! Yuzu-<i>chan</i>?

00:18:08.330 --> 00:18:12.300
I see. It must be hard on your own.

00:18:12.300 --> 00:18:15.670
We'll look for her, too, as we go.

00:18:15.670 --> 00:18:18.930
It's all right. I'm sure she'll turn up!

00:18:18.930 --> 00:18:21.220
Here, Tamahiko-<i>kun</i>--eat these.

00:18:21.220 --> 00:18:22.930
Huh? But...

00:18:22.930 --> 00:18:26.390
You haven't eaten a thing, have you?
These'll give you a boost!

00:18:28.690 --> 00:18:30.060
Thank you.

00:18:30.060 --> 00:18:32.610
Aw, why so polite?

00:18:32.610 --> 00:18:33.980
--We're friends!
--We're friends!

00:18:37.820 --> 00:18:39.820
When was it?

00:18:39.820 --> 00:18:42.120
When did I stop being alone?

00:18:43.490 --> 00:18:45.950
Such grueling circumstances, and yet...

00:18:45.950 --> 00:18:49.120
...everyone's in such fine spirits.

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:53.130
And all because Yuzu the
spring storm has blown through.

00:18:54.380 --> 00:18:57.090
You've brought me so much joy.

00:18:58.510 --> 00:19:01.590
Now for me to make <i>you </i>happy.

00:19:01.590 --> 00:19:04.350
So please... let's get home soon!

00:19:06.390 --> 00:19:09.640
I'd like to have another, but...
I'll hold off.

00:19:12.860 --> 00:19:13.820
Hey!

00:19:15.360 --> 00:19:17.360
Wait up, big bwother!

00:19:20.610 --> 00:19:21.660
Yoko!

00:19:24.370 --> 00:19:26.080
I-I'm sorry!

00:19:26.080 --> 00:19:30.000
I'll give them back, just--
please, don't hit my little sister!

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:32.790
I'm sowwy!

00:19:32.790 --> 00:19:37.010
What a coincidence.
I have a little sister, too.

00:19:37.010 --> 00:19:41.010
You can have them, out of my
respect for you protecting her.

00:19:41.010 --> 00:19:42.890
Huh? Are you sure?

00:19:42.890 --> 00:19:44.640
Yes.

00:19:44.640 --> 00:19:45.970
Thank you!

00:19:45.970 --> 00:19:47.100
Fanks!

00:19:55.190 --> 00:20:00.150
We got separated from our mom
and dad--with nothing to eat.

00:20:00.150 --> 00:20:01.780
That's rough.

00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:06.870
Big Sis was wif us, too,
but she fell down. I'm worried.

00:20:08.240 --> 00:20:09.910
Another child?

00:20:09.910 --> 00:20:13.080
Let's take her to the first-aid site.
Where is she?

00:20:14.830 --> 00:20:16.460
She's in here.

00:20:16.460 --> 00:20:20.130
You hid her here?
This could collapse at any moment.

00:20:20.130 --> 00:20:22.470
It was the best place we could find.

00:20:22.470 --> 00:20:27.680
It must have been so hard--three young
siblings without your parents.

00:20:27.680 --> 00:20:30.140
Big Sis isn't really our sister.

00:20:30.140 --> 00:20:31.140
Eh?

00:20:31.140 --> 00:20:34.730
She helped Yoko when she started crying.

00:20:35.900 --> 00:20:38.900
An' she tied this wibbon for me!

00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:40.940
You don't say. Cute!

00:20:40.940 --> 00:20:42.070
Uh-huh!

00:20:42.070 --> 00:20:44.610
I wuv Big Sis Yuzuki!

00:20:50.410 --> 00:20:51.580
Yuzu...

00:20:51.580 --> 00:20:52.580
Yuzu!

00:20:53.160 --> 00:20:54.170
Yuzu!

00:20:55.750 --> 00:20:56.790
Yuzu!

00:21:02.670 --> 00:21:04.430
Yuzu!

00:21:04.430 --> 00:21:08.180
Say, mister, are you Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>?

00:21:08.180 --> 00:21:09.560
How did you...

00:21:09.560 --> 00:21:14.480
She's been mumbling to herself, all
"Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>"...

00:21:17.690 --> 00:21:18.980
Listen up, okay?

00:21:18.980 --> 00:21:23.610
If you walk a little toward Jinbocho,
you'll see Kotori Shiratori.

00:21:23.610 --> 00:21:24.400
--Wow!
--Wow!

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:25.610
Kotowi-<i>chan</i>!

00:21:25.610 --> 00:21:29.580
You two go there and tell her you met me.

00:21:29.580 --> 00:21:32.620
I'm sure my friends will help out.

00:21:36.830 --> 00:21:41.340
Sorry--could you use this to tie Yuzu
real tight to my right hand?

00:21:41.340 --> 00:21:42.590
S-Sure!

00:21:45.510 --> 00:21:47.970
Tamahiko... <i>sama</i>...

00:21:52.970 --> 00:21:55.850
Yuzu... Yuzu...

00:21:55.850 --> 00:22:00.110
Your warm body is right here
in my arms, breathing...

00:22:02.110 --> 00:22:04.070
Thank God you're alive!

00:23:45.550 --> 00:23:48.510
--In the end: a spring storm.
--In the end: a spring storm.
